WEBVTT

00:32.114 --> 00:36.160
FIFTIES PROFESSIONALS

00:36.244 --> 00:40.623
10 YEARS AGO

00:41.374 --> 00:43.125
EPISODE 2

00:56.013 --> 00:57.598
Excuse me.

01:05.231 --> 01:06.315
Hello...

01:08.317 --> 01:09.652
Ms. Shibasaki?

01:22.999 --> 01:24.083
Shit!

01:24.333 --> 01:25.334
Black Pearl.

01:25.918 --> 01:27.795
You've developed a foul mouth
since we last met.

01:35.428 --> 01:36.679
Bulgae...

01:37.972 --> 01:40.600
You son of a bitch.

02:23.934 --> 02:25.353
RESCUE EQUIPMENT BOX

02:37.573 --> 02:38.991
Hands up and get up slowly.

02:47.500 --> 02:49.001
I'd only heard rumors about you.

02:50.086 --> 02:51.796
I never thought Bulgae would be a woman.

02:53.047 --> 02:54.465
Don't try anything funny

02:54.757 --> 02:55.883
and hand over the bag.

03:24.120 --> 03:25.287
Check the bathroom.

03:31.836 --> 03:33.087
- Boss.
- What is it?

03:38.676 --> 03:39.802
Damn it.

03:41.053 --> 03:42.054
- Hey, Gong-bok.
- Yes, sir.

03:42.138 --> 03:43.305
Keep an eye on them

03:43.389 --> 03:44.557
- and toss every room.
- Yes, sir.

03:46.600 --> 03:47.810
Well? Are you going to hand it over?

04:55.503 --> 04:56.629
What the hell are you?

04:56.962 --> 04:58.088
You're a man?

04:58.172 --> 05:00.382
So you're not completely blind after all.

05:00.508 --> 05:01.926
And you're supposed to be
North Korea's top agent?

05:02.468 --> 05:03.761
What the hell? That's just perverted!

05:03.844 --> 05:06.096
Ever heard of an operational disguise?

05:06.180 --> 05:07.932
I don't care if it's for an operation.

05:08.724 --> 05:10.768
Damn it. When you lifted your leg...

05:14.313 --> 05:16.190
How disgusting. I can't exactly fight
with my eyes closed.

05:16.732 --> 05:18.150
You could've at least shaved!

05:18.776 --> 05:20.236
Are you all talk?

05:21.570 --> 05:23.614
Enough talk and come at me.

07:34.453 --> 07:36.497
You damn son of a bitch.

08:04.858 --> 08:05.859
What are you doing?

08:05.943 --> 08:07.444
Hurry and pull me up!

08:49.028 --> 08:53.532
FIFTIES PROFESSIONALS

09:00.998 --> 09:01.999
Damn it.

09:26.565 --> 09:29.443
Who the hell are you, you bastard?

09:31.570 --> 09:32.696
You bastard.

09:32.821 --> 09:33.822
Uncle.

09:41.330 --> 09:42.414
HEO NAM-IL, 64 HAGEUN-RO, YEONGSAN-GUN

09:46.293 --> 09:47.294
Let's go.

09:49.463 --> 09:50.631
You bastard.

10:00.474 --> 10:01.517
What the hell...

10:32.381 --> 10:33.799
HEAVEN HOTEL

10:36.760 --> 10:39.012
IMCHEON DISTRICT PROSECUTORS' OFFICE

10:44.226 --> 10:46.145
The only thing on the USB you gave us

10:46.353 --> 10:48.188
was this CCTV footage, Prosecutor.

10:49.356 --> 10:52.568
A ferry from 2016.

10:56.321 --> 10:58.198
This article seems to be from
around that time.

10:59.741 --> 11:01.702
The footage and the gun...

11:02.411 --> 11:03.871
What kind of person

11:03.954 --> 11:06.331
builds a secret room
just to hide things like this?

11:06.456 --> 11:08.125
She was no ordinary civilian.

11:08.625 --> 11:10.252
The pistol from that room

11:10.502 --> 11:12.713
is a Russian model used
by North Korean soldiers.

11:13.714 --> 11:15.632
So, the dead woman
was a North Korean soldier...

11:16.008 --> 11:17.217
Is that what you mean?

11:20.554 --> 11:22.973
But why would a woman like her
commit suicide in our country?

11:24.558 --> 11:25.893
Rather than a suicide

11:26.226 --> 11:29.521
it's more likely she was murdered
after being exposed in a NewTube video.

11:29.605 --> 11:31.064
That's a more plausible theory.

11:31.481 --> 11:33.483
It seemed like she was living in hiding.

11:33.692 --> 11:35.194
Laying low

11:35.569 --> 11:37.279
and going through the data here.

11:38.363 --> 11:39.364
Let's start

11:39.448 --> 11:42.075
by identifying the people
in the CCTV footage.

11:42.284 --> 11:44.119
We need to get the passenger list
from the ferry.

11:44.328 --> 11:45.329
Yes, ma'am.

11:49.958 --> 11:51.251
Yes, this is Prosecutor Gang Yeong-ae.

11:51.919 --> 11:52.920
Yes, Chief Prosecutor.

11:54.838 --> 11:55.839
Right now?

11:57.174 --> 11:58.175
Prosecutor Gang.

11:58.508 --> 11:59.593
are you out of your mind?

12:00.010 --> 12:01.428
You just got transferred

12:01.595 --> 12:03.222
and you're already reopening a closed case

12:03.305 --> 12:04.848
that you decided on your own

12:05.349 --> 12:06.433
to go to the scene?

12:07.267 --> 12:08.936
When you go around
stirring things up like that

12:09.061 --> 12:11.021
do you know
what they say about prosecutors?

12:11.104 --> 12:14.524
That they're just giving
hard-working cops the runaround!

12:16.485 --> 12:17.861
Have you not heard that?

12:20.656 --> 12:21.657
I have not.

12:23.992 --> 12:25.202
I was not aware of that.

12:28.080 --> 12:29.373
What? You weren't aware?

12:30.624 --> 12:32.084
Oh, I am terribly sorry.

12:32.167 --> 12:34.086
I guess I, once again,
failed to read the room.

12:35.671 --> 12:37.547
I let my eagerness get the better of me.

12:38.090 --> 12:40.217
I am so very sorry

12:40.634 --> 12:41.635
for causing you this trouble.

12:42.970 --> 12:44.888
Whether it's a written reprimand
or a pay cut

12:45.764 --> 12:46.765
I'll accept it.

12:49.726 --> 12:50.769
This one time...

12:51.228 --> 12:53.397
I'll let it slide and take the blame.

12:54.147 --> 12:55.148
But this case...

12:55.732 --> 12:57.109
If I hear that Prosecutor Gang

12:57.776 --> 13:00.153
is poking around again

13:00.404 --> 13:03.073
I'll have you transferred to some
backwater branch office.

13:04.074 --> 13:05.075
Yes, sir.

13:12.958 --> 13:15.419
I made sure she won't go

13:15.502 --> 13:17.254
near the case again.

13:20.716 --> 13:22.342
The new troublemaker

13:22.592 --> 13:24.928
seems to have gotten a bit overzealous.

13:25.304 --> 13:26.596
Are you sure?

13:27.180 --> 13:28.307
Yes.

13:28.390 --> 13:31.310
Well, I've already gotten the police
on the same page.

13:31.768 --> 13:34.062
What could possibly happen now?

13:35.981 --> 13:39.609
I should be treating you
to a meal in person

13:39.985 --> 13:40.986
but it's election season.

13:41.528 --> 13:42.654
Instead, tonight

13:43.196 --> 13:45.490
I'll send my regards through Chief Baek.

13:45.991 --> 13:46.992
All right.

13:54.207 --> 13:55.500
Representative Kim Jung-hyeok is here.

13:55.834 --> 13:57.294
- Show him in.
- Yes, sir.

14:00.756 --> 14:02.341
Goodness.

14:02.549 --> 14:05.135
You've got a great view here, huh?

14:05.886 --> 14:08.138
You can see all of Imcheon from up here.

14:08.347 --> 14:10.182
It's quite a sight, isn't it?

14:11.016 --> 14:12.017
You're too kind.

14:14.144 --> 14:17.522
FLOOR LEADER OF THE SAEHANJIN PARTY,
KIM JUNG-HYEOK

14:18.440 --> 14:21.985
But you know, standing here like this...

14:22.986 --> 14:26.198
there's one thing I just don't understand.

14:28.283 --> 14:30.118
Why would the great Han Gyeong-wook

14:30.243 --> 14:32.704
give up this office with its amazing view

14:32.871 --> 14:34.247
and be so desperate

14:34.331 --> 14:36.666
to get into
that run-down city hall building?

14:37.084 --> 14:38.835
What's in it for you

14:38.919 --> 14:40.295
being the mayor of some backwater town?

14:41.088 --> 14:42.589
Besides, in Imcheon

14:42.923 --> 14:44.925
Kim Seon-jung, who's also running

14:45.008 --> 14:46.760
has the place on lock.

14:46.843 --> 14:49.179
To go out of your way
to turn down an easy path

14:49.429 --> 14:50.972
and wade through filth

14:51.181 --> 14:53.642
just to run in this election...

14:54.434 --> 14:57.562
There must be a very good reason.

14:58.563 --> 15:01.233
Why don't we sit
and discuss it over some tea?

15:01.316 --> 15:03.193
I just got some excellent tea in.

15:04.945 --> 15:06.196
Look.

15:06.613 --> 15:07.823
During election season

15:07.906 --> 15:09.574
do you think you're the only one

15:09.658 --> 15:11.118
inviting me for tea?

15:11.451 --> 15:12.953
After you give me an answer

15:13.036 --> 15:15.497
I'll decide whether or not
to have that tea.

15:15.580 --> 15:16.623
Well...

15:17.541 --> 15:19.918
Your insight is truly unparalleled, sir.

15:22.587 --> 15:23.797
Sir, have you ever...

15:24.214 --> 15:25.924
heard of Yeongseon Island?

15:26.091 --> 15:27.300
Yeongseon Island?

15:27.801 --> 15:29.845
You mean, because of one island

15:29.970 --> 15:31.138
you started this whole thing?

15:31.221 --> 15:33.515
Let me explain it in a way
that's easy to understand.

15:33.849 --> 15:34.850
Please, have a seat.

15:35.142 --> 15:36.143
Yeongseon Island

15:36.726 --> 15:38.353
is a bit far from the mainland

15:38.603 --> 15:41.481
but with major Northeast Asian countries
like China and Japan

15:41.606 --> 15:42.732
it's a geographical strongpoint

15:42.816 --> 15:45.068
perfectly optimized for maritime trade.

15:45.485 --> 15:46.903
Its tourism resources aren't bad either.

15:47.154 --> 15:48.405
The only downside is

15:48.822 --> 15:50.740
it's tied up in too many regulations

15:50.824 --> 15:53.160
for environmental and domestic protection.

15:53.493 --> 15:54.744
Because of that, right now,

15:54.828 --> 15:57.414
there's only one casino
for locals barely operating.

15:57.497 --> 16:00.792
But if we let wealthy foreigners run
businesses there without regulations...

16:00.959 --> 16:02.419
If we loosen what needs to be loosened

16:02.502 --> 16:03.920
and turn a blind eye to what we must

16:04.087 --> 16:05.172
what do you think will happen?

16:05.797 --> 16:07.674
Yeongseon Island could easily

16:07.757 --> 16:10.010
become the biggest pleasure
island in Asia.

16:10.927 --> 16:12.012
You don't mean...

16:12.429 --> 16:14.764
- Already?
- For tourism developers in Northeast Asia

16:14.848 --> 16:15.891
Yeongseon Island

16:15.974 --> 16:18.685
is the perfect location
to use as a business hub.

16:18.977 --> 16:21.813
Many companies have already
expressed their interest in participating.

16:22.397 --> 16:23.940
If we sell off pieces of the island

16:24.441 --> 16:27.652
we could generate
a profit of about 25 trillion won.

16:27.903 --> 16:30.489
25... 25 trillion?

16:30.655 --> 16:31.698
With that kind of money

16:31.781 --> 16:34.868
for you to become president in four years

16:35.911 --> 16:37.621
wouldn't that be a good stepping stone?

16:37.871 --> 16:40.457
Do you really think this will pan out
the way you've imagined?

16:41.124 --> 16:43.919
I mean, Kim Seon-jung
will be tough to deal with.

16:44.044 --> 16:45.879
If you would just give it a little push

16:46.379 --> 16:47.964
wouldn't things go much more smoothly?

16:54.054 --> 16:56.014
Oh, right. Is that tea ready?

16:56.389 --> 16:57.599
I heard you got something special.

17:06.441 --> 17:09.027
This was sold to China by Kim Jong-il
during the Arduous March.

17:09.611 --> 17:10.904
It's a bronze ewer.

17:12.322 --> 17:15.033
I acquired it through a connection
from my time at the NIS.

17:15.867 --> 17:17.202
If you'll allow me

17:17.285 --> 17:19.246
I'd like to present it to you as a gift.

17:20.288 --> 17:21.623
Will you accept it?

18:03.832 --> 18:06.167
This is the woman
Kim Jung-hyeok has been seeing lately.

18:06.543 --> 18:08.878
He gifted her a three-story café building
in Gangnam behind his family's back

18:09.087 --> 18:11.089
and it looks like there was
some tax evasion involved.

18:15.093 --> 18:17.345
We need that to keep a leash
on the old geezer

18:17.429 --> 18:18.847
- so keep it safe.
- Yes, sir.

18:19.139 --> 18:20.223
By the way.

18:20.473 --> 18:22.934
How's the land acquisition
on Yeongseon Island coming along?

18:23.018 --> 18:24.519
Due to strong opposition
from the residents

18:24.603 --> 18:25.895
it's been slightly delayed.

18:25.979 --> 18:27.480
Yoo In-gu went down to handle it himself

18:27.564 --> 18:29.107
- so if you'll just wait...
- Joong-ki.

18:30.150 --> 18:31.401
You're taking too long.

18:32.277 --> 18:33.278
Get it?

18:35.155 --> 18:36.197
My apologies.

18:36.489 --> 18:38.033
I'll instruct them to push
this forward as much as possible.

18:46.916 --> 18:50.170
Hey, I told you to just put your
thumbprint on it so we can finish up.

18:50.712 --> 18:52.505
I said that's our ancestral land

18:52.756 --> 18:54.674
so it's not for sale.

18:54.799 --> 18:57.052
This old fool still doesn't get it.

18:57.135 --> 18:59.554
Look, the money I borrowed...

18:59.638 --> 19:01.806
I'll take care of it this week.

19:01.890 --> 19:03.391
- Please...
- Hey, he hasn't had enough.

19:03.475 --> 19:04.476
Get him.

19:06.645 --> 19:08.313
Kkot-nim. Business going well?

19:08.396 --> 19:09.439
Hello, boss!

19:10.273 --> 19:11.691
You should've called before you came.

19:11.775 --> 19:12.776
What brings you here?

19:12.859 --> 19:14.903
I've gotta make it look like I'm doing
something, right?

19:15.028 --> 19:17.280
Chief Han is raising hell,
telling us to get a move on.

19:18.156 --> 19:19.783
Boss, you know we're on it.

19:19.866 --> 19:22.285
- Sector A will be wrapped up soon.
- So I see.

19:22.827 --> 19:25.121
- Are you doing what I told you?
- Of course, boss.

19:47.769 --> 19:50.689
Jeez, the jerky business is booming, huh?

19:52.273 --> 19:55.360
But boss, are you sure it's okay to be
running a business behind his back?

19:55.819 --> 19:57.570
Chief Han is not someone
to be trifled with.

19:58.363 --> 19:59.906
Hey, that guy's too busy

19:59.989 --> 20:02.200
driving around in that truck
giving speeches.

20:03.201 --> 20:05.787
We're going to get a big cut once the
Yeongseon Island deal is done anyway,

20:06.371 --> 20:08.289
so I'm worried this is just stirring up
unnecessary trouble.

20:08.915 --> 20:11.042
You loyal bastard.

20:11.501 --> 20:13.128
Just wait until this Yeongseon Island deal
is done.

20:13.211 --> 20:15.380
You think that viper Chief Han
and that vixen Chairman Do

20:15.463 --> 20:17.966
are going to reward their underlings
for a job well done?

20:18.383 --> 20:21.052
We'll be lucky if they don't
trump up a charge and screw us over.

20:21.469 --> 20:22.762
Before that

20:22.846 --> 20:25.724
we need to grab everything we can.

20:25.932 --> 20:27.642
If we don't want to end up empty-handed.

20:29.352 --> 20:30.562
So that was your grand plan.

20:30.895 --> 20:31.896
Boss!

20:32.772 --> 20:34.149
There's a problem at the capital firm.

20:57.881 --> 20:58.882
What's this?

21:00.175 --> 21:01.176
My arm...

21:04.763 --> 21:05.930
Why won't my arm move?

21:08.475 --> 21:09.517
Uncle, Uncle!

21:10.351 --> 21:11.352
Are you okay?

21:14.230 --> 21:15.398
Shouldn't you still be in bed?

21:15.732 --> 21:17.984
When...

21:18.860 --> 21:20.695
did I get home?

21:21.946 --> 21:23.573
I remember going for the house deed

21:23.656 --> 21:25.492
and getting beaten up

21:26.075 --> 21:27.243
but that's it.

21:27.577 --> 21:29.621
Uncle, don't worry about the deed.

21:30.163 --> 21:31.539
I got them all back.

21:34.000 --> 21:35.001
Those bastards.

21:35.418 --> 21:38.755
Looks like they're determined to bleed the
people of Yeongseon Island dry.

21:40.673 --> 21:42.342
CERTIFIED COPY OF REAL ESTATE REGISTRY
BUILDING

21:42.425 --> 21:43.802
How did you get these back?

21:45.428 --> 21:46.429
What?

21:47.764 --> 21:48.807
You don't remember?

21:49.724 --> 21:50.725
No.

21:53.728 --> 21:56.147
I remember getting hit really hard once.

21:57.398 --> 21:58.983
After that one big hit...

22:02.362 --> 22:03.404
What happened?

22:07.534 --> 22:10.119
My whole body is aching.
Did I get beat up badly?

22:11.371 --> 22:12.497
Uncle.

22:12.831 --> 22:14.958
Getting beat up
isn't what matters right now.

22:16.501 --> 22:17.585
But, why are you...

22:19.128 --> 22:20.463
calling me "Uncle"?

22:21.589 --> 22:23.174
Not "Hey, you" like before.

22:24.843 --> 22:28.513
Oh, that's because I didn't really know
you back then.

22:30.098 --> 22:33.268
I'm telling you, it was like
watching a martial arts movie.

22:33.518 --> 22:35.728
- You're saying that's me?
- Yeah!

22:36.354 --> 22:38.147
All of a sudden, you just snapped.

22:38.231 --> 22:39.232
You were, like...

22:41.067 --> 22:42.235
And after a few moves

22:42.318 --> 22:43.736
you just wiped the floor with them.

22:45.738 --> 22:46.906
I don't remember any of that.

22:49.158 --> 22:51.619
Are you sure you're not lying to cover up
something you did?

22:51.953 --> 22:53.037
Come on

22:53.121 --> 22:55.248
why would I make something like that up?

22:55.748 --> 22:56.875
Watch again. See?

23:02.213 --> 23:03.214
How can that be me?

23:03.298 --> 23:04.966
I think when things got dangerous

23:05.049 --> 23:07.093
your hidden past must have come out.

23:08.344 --> 23:10.305
- A hidden past?
- Yeah.

23:10.388 --> 23:12.265
You know, like in the movies.

23:12.473 --> 23:13.933
When the hero is in danger

23:14.017 --> 23:16.936
their past just suddenly
comes flashing back.

23:17.520 --> 23:19.647
Anything coming back to you, Uncle?

23:21.190 --> 23:22.483
No, my head just hurts.

23:24.027 --> 23:27.155
So I came up with a theory.

23:27.614 --> 23:29.407
Who are you really, Uncle?

23:29.866 --> 23:31.075
How can you be such a good fighter?

23:33.036 --> 23:34.329
And the answer became obvious.

23:35.914 --> 23:36.998
A 007 agent.

23:37.874 --> 23:39.208
And I never said it

23:39.292 --> 23:40.877
but I always thought the vibe you give off

23:41.085 --> 23:42.879
was really intense.

23:45.423 --> 23:47.175
I suppose I do have that side to me.

23:50.511 --> 23:52.263
Is it that obvious to you?

23:53.139 --> 23:54.307
Yeah, I'm telling you!

23:56.517 --> 23:57.644
Bulgae showed up!

23:57.727 --> 24:00.355
- It was Bulgae!
- Hey, Ho-myeong, calm down.

24:00.772 --> 24:02.607
Seong-won, run a trace
on a motorcycle plate.

24:02.690 --> 24:04.943
It's Imcheon, Yeongseon-ga

24:05.151 --> 24:06.569
- 9342.
- Hey, Jeong Ho-myeong!

24:06.653 --> 24:08.780
No, on second thought, you get down here.
We'll look for him together.

24:08.863 --> 24:10.782
The more you rush,
the more careful you have to be.

24:10.865 --> 24:12.283
Have you already forgotten
what happened that day, ten years ago?

24:15.370 --> 24:16.371
Ho-myeong

24:16.454 --> 24:18.748
I'll get you the plate search
results by tomorrow morning.

24:19.040 --> 24:20.416
You need to confirm
whether that guy is really Bulgae

24:20.500 --> 24:22.043
and if he actually has the goods.

24:22.126 --> 24:23.878
Focus on that first. All right?

24:24.087 --> 24:26.089
I'll finish up here and be right there.

24:26.631 --> 24:28.174
Okay? Be smart about this.

24:28.841 --> 24:30.176
- All right.
- Okay.

24:32.470 --> 24:35.306
- That Jeong Ho-myeong...
- Hey, mister!

24:35.890 --> 24:37.475
So, when's it going to be ready?

24:38.017 --> 24:39.435
Oh, yes. It'll be right out.

24:40.436 --> 24:42.230
- Good grief.
- I'm sorry.

24:42.772 --> 24:46.109
How long do I have to wait
for just one of these things? Seriously.

24:50.697 --> 24:52.031
Get out.

24:52.115 --> 24:54.158
I'm sorry, boss. I messed up, boss.

24:54.242 --> 24:56.119
- I just...
- Get out.

25:00.415 --> 25:01.666
Wait a minute. For real.

25:01.749 --> 25:03.334
Hold still, you bastard,
before you get hurt.

25:03.459 --> 25:05.003
It really hurts. It hurts so much.

25:05.086 --> 25:07.922
And the spot where that guy
hit me earlier still hurts like hell.

25:08.840 --> 25:10.967
You lose all the deeds
we worked so hard to collect

25:11.050 --> 25:12.343
and now you're complaining
that you're in pain?

25:12.760 --> 25:15.096
I'm telling you, he was no ordinary guy.

25:15.680 --> 25:18.641
The way his body was just flying around...

25:18.725 --> 25:20.518
He was like a martial arts master.

25:20.601 --> 25:22.186
And the other guy, the one in the hat...

25:22.270 --> 25:24.230
his hands and feet were unbelievably fast.

25:24.480 --> 25:26.691
It made me wonder what guys like them were
doing in a backwater place like this.

25:26.774 --> 25:28.443
For real.

25:29.235 --> 25:31.112
What are you doing,
writing a restaurant review?

25:32.071 --> 25:34.157
- So how many stars?
- A lot... Wait, I'm sorry.

25:34.699 --> 25:36.409
Hey, you goddamn morons!

25:36.492 --> 25:38.036
If you're going to come back after getting
your asses handed to you

25:38.119 --> 25:41.122
you should've at least brought back a
video or a photo of the bastard's face!

25:41.205 --> 25:42.874
Come on, you know how it is, Boss.

25:43.291 --> 25:45.168
Our security cameras are just for show.

25:45.251 --> 25:47.170
In case any issues came up later

25:47.503 --> 25:49.839
you're the one who told us not to install
real cameras at the loan office.

25:49.922 --> 25:51.591
Don't you remember ordering that yourself?

25:52.175 --> 25:53.384
Right. So now it's my fault?

25:54.677 --> 25:55.678
- Hold it out.
- Yes, sir.

25:58.264 --> 26:00.016
Wait, that really hurts!

26:00.099 --> 26:01.100
I'm so sorry...

26:04.145 --> 26:05.229
All of you, get up!

26:05.313 --> 26:07.315
Oh, what do I do?

26:11.736 --> 26:12.820
- Hey.
- Yes, sir.

26:13.362 --> 26:15.198
Go sweet-talk the hotel security team

26:15.281 --> 26:16.574
and get the lobby's CCTV footage.

26:17.283 --> 26:18.743
Do it quietly, without Chairman Do
finding out.

26:18.993 --> 26:20.912
Why without Chairman Do finding out?

26:21.037 --> 26:22.872
Hey, you idiot. Can't you think?

26:23.039 --> 26:24.957
Chairman Do is just dying to
get rid of us.

26:25.041 --> 26:26.542
If she finds out this happened

26:27.251 --> 26:28.669
do you think she'd just let us be?

26:28.920 --> 26:31.464
And if word gets out about trouble at one
of our spots, and Chief Han hears about it

26:31.547 --> 26:33.382
- don't you know we're finished?
- Right.

26:35.176 --> 26:36.344
You have three days

26:36.427 --> 26:38.262
to catch those bastards
and drag them here to me.

26:38.930 --> 26:40.264
I don't care if he's a martial arts
master or just some guy in a cap.

26:40.348 --> 26:41.516
I'll kill him myself.

26:41.766 --> 26:42.767
Yes, I understand, Boss.

26:43.518 --> 26:44.977
Answer, you bastards! Damn it.

26:45.061 --> 26:46.104
- Yes, Boss!
- Yes, Boss!

26:46.896 --> 26:47.980
But, Boss...

26:48.940 --> 26:49.941
Where do I find them?

26:52.777 --> 26:54.862
- You want me to put it in your GPS?
- I'm sorry.

26:55.238 --> 26:57.156
What are you waiting for? Go! Now!

26:57.448 --> 26:59.325
Let's go! Come on, let's move!

26:59.408 --> 27:00.409
Damn it!

27:01.285 --> 27:02.286
I'm serious.

27:02.370 --> 27:04.580
The loan sharks were all beaten to a pulp.

27:06.082 --> 27:07.083
So?

27:07.166 --> 27:08.209
What do you mean, so?

27:08.668 --> 27:11.254
This is a guy who hasn't gotten a single
speeding ticket in ten years.

27:11.337 --> 27:13.047
He must've had a reason for making a move.

27:13.923 --> 27:15.383
Let's put him under 24-hour surveillance

27:15.466 --> 27:16.467
and get to the bottom of this.

27:16.592 --> 27:18.928
If you're on 24-hour surveillance,
what about our 24-hour convenience store?

27:20.096 --> 27:21.264
Well, we'll have to close up shop.

27:21.347 --> 27:23.641
That's fine by me.
I was getting sick of this place anyway.

27:23.975 --> 27:25.184
Jeez, Gong-bok.

27:25.476 --> 27:27.603
Were you late for your shift

27:27.687 --> 27:28.729
because you were doing this useless stuff?

27:28.813 --> 27:30.398
Who cares about my shift right now?

27:30.481 --> 27:31.732
He's made his move.

27:31.816 --> 27:33.901
The guy we've been watching for ten years.

27:34.026 --> 27:37.113
Our Boss, who was framed and sent to
prison, all our scattered guys...

27:37.196 --> 27:39.824
This could be our one chance to get it all
back. Why are you hesitating?

27:39.907 --> 27:41.742
I'm asking why he would suddenly make a
move now!

27:41.826 --> 27:42.827
There's no reason for it!

27:42.910 --> 27:44.537
That's what I'm saying we should find out.

27:45.079 --> 27:47.039
Come on. You never used to hesitate.
What's wrong?

27:49.250 --> 27:52.545
Oh, I know. It's because of that cop,
isn't it? That lady cop.

27:54.463 --> 27:55.464
What?

27:57.508 --> 27:58.509
Well...

28:03.222 --> 28:05.600
Wow. Unbelievable.

28:06.058 --> 28:07.059
Hey.

28:07.435 --> 28:10.021
In what convenience store does the
part-timer spy on the owner, huh?

28:11.981 --> 28:13.065
What did you just say?

28:13.191 --> 28:14.275
- Part-timer?
- Yep.

28:15.443 --> 28:17.570
- Am I just a part-timer at this store?
- Yeah.

28:19.488 --> 28:20.948
Okay, I see how you really feel.

28:21.157 --> 28:22.158
As for Jeong Ho-myeong

28:22.241 --> 28:25.036
I'll keep a close watch on him by myself.

28:28.831 --> 28:30.833
Go, just go! Fine, go.

28:30.917 --> 28:32.043
Hey, pay for that!

28:32.501 --> 28:34.295
Wait, don't go!
You have to take over for me!

28:35.213 --> 28:37.215
I just pulled an all-nighter!

29:37.066 --> 29:38.234
Nice shot.

29:45.491 --> 29:46.534
CONVERTING TO MULTIMEDIA MESSAGE...

29:50.204 --> 29:53.332
Yes, Chief Kim. I just sent you a license
plate number. That's right.

29:54.041 --> 29:55.668
I have a favor to ask.

29:56.168 --> 29:58.963
ORAN CHINESE RESTAURANT

30:07.221 --> 30:08.472
Why isn't he here yet?

30:11.225 --> 30:13.352
Still no word from Ho-myeong?

30:13.436 --> 30:15.813
Ho-myeong isn't capable
of collecting that debt.

30:16.188 --> 30:18.316
He'll be lucky if he doesn't get beaten up
by those thugs.

30:25.364 --> 30:27.158
Hey, looks like they didn't beat you up
too badly.

30:27.241 --> 30:29.035
- Why weren't you answering your phone?
- What about the tab?

30:29.452 --> 30:30.453
Did you get it?

30:31.412 --> 30:32.705
I'm a little tired.

30:33.205 --> 30:34.582
I'm going to go upstairs and rest.

30:35.249 --> 30:36.250
Hey, wait.

30:43.215 --> 30:44.383
See? I told you.

30:44.467 --> 30:46.052
I told you it was
too much for him, didn't I?

30:51.474 --> 30:54.602
Jeez, if a man is going to
go out there with some grit

30:54.810 --> 30:56.937
he should at least come back with a few
bucks.

30:58.272 --> 31:00.941
Dad, you really don't know your
son-in-law at all, do you?

31:01.400 --> 31:04.278
From now on, absolutely no orders from
Heaven Capital.

31:04.445 --> 31:05.946
- Got it?
- Yeah, okay.

31:06.489 --> 31:07.490
Mister!

31:07.573 --> 31:08.699
- You got that?
- I got it.

31:20.586 --> 31:22.046
The more you rush,
the more careful you have to be.

31:23.047 --> 31:24.507
Have you already forgotten
what happened that day, ten years ago?

31:27.426 --> 31:29.261
You go to Yeongseon Island
and find Bulgae, okay?

31:29.345 --> 31:31.555
- Just find him.
- It's dangerous for you to go alone.

31:31.639 --> 31:32.932
- Let me go...
- No, don't come.

31:33.432 --> 31:35.935
Don't come and just lay low
until I contact you, all right?

31:36.018 --> 31:37.019
I'll be in touch.

31:59.834 --> 32:01.043
Han Gyeong-wook.

32:02.002 --> 32:03.754
Are you calling your superior by his name?

32:04.880 --> 32:06.132
Did you forget the chain of command?

32:07.550 --> 32:09.218
Han Gyeong-wook, you son of a bitch.

32:20.020 --> 32:22.731
So much for Team Leader Jo,
the champion of justice.

32:23.190 --> 32:25.734
Shaking in your boots
over a few measly bullets.

32:28.404 --> 32:29.864
I'll give you a chance to live.

32:30.448 --> 32:31.532
The location of the item...

32:31.991 --> 32:33.492
you guys know it, don't you?

32:33.993 --> 32:35.369
Did Jeong Ho-myeong come looking for it?

32:36.245 --> 32:37.288
Why?

32:40.249 --> 32:41.625
Even the great Han Gyeong-wook...

32:42.209 --> 32:43.210
is getting scared, I see.

32:46.172 --> 32:47.423
All right, fine.

32:47.506 --> 32:50.009
Well, if I get Jeong Ho-myeong here
and ask him myself

32:50.092 --> 32:51.343
I'm sure I'll get an answer.

32:51.427 --> 32:53.929
Yeah, good luck with that.

32:54.805 --> 32:57.641
You trained him,
so you know him best, right?

32:57.725 --> 32:59.435
Of course, I do.

32:59.518 --> 33:01.270
I know exactly what kind
of man Jeong Ho-myeong is.

33:02.646 --> 33:03.772
In terms of pure skill

33:03.856 --> 33:06.567
he's the best there is.

33:08.694 --> 33:10.863
But his weakness is
that he cares too much.

33:15.367 --> 33:18.829
Jeong Ho-myeong is fiercely l
oyal to his senior.

33:18.913 --> 33:20.873
If he hears that
Team Leader Jo Seong-won is dead

33:21.832 --> 33:23.042
he will show up

33:23.292 --> 33:25.252
at the funeral no matter what.

33:25.711 --> 33:26.712
Am I wrong?

33:36.222 --> 33:37.431
Looks like the counter-intelligence agents
have arrived.

33:38.224 --> 33:39.225
We should pull out now.

33:44.063 --> 33:45.147
Let's fall back for now.

33:45.231 --> 33:47.233
Post our agents
at all the places he might go.

33:47.608 --> 33:48.609
Understood.

33:54.573 --> 33:56.075
I won't lose him this time.

33:57.117 --> 33:58.118
Never.

33:58.827 --> 34:01.372
NIS AGENT MISSING... INTERNAL MANAGEMENT
FLAWS EXPOSED AT INTELLIGENCE AGENCY

34:14.176 --> 34:15.553
103BEO 8589

34:22.726 --> 34:25.813
- Yes, Chief Kim.
- I tailed the car like you asked.

34:25.896 --> 34:27.398
But do you really...

34:28.232 --> 34:29.275
need to know this?

34:29.358 --> 34:30.985
You couldn't track the owner's movements?

34:31.068 --> 34:32.194
No, that's not it.

34:32.278 --> 34:33.362
The owner of the car is...

34:36.073 --> 34:37.408
Han Gyeong-wook's secretary.

34:39.326 --> 34:40.369
Han Gyeong-wook?

34:41.495 --> 34:42.538
Yes.

34:43.664 --> 34:46.000
Han Gyeong-wook, the one running
for Mayor of Imcheon.

34:49.753 --> 34:50.796
Prosecutor.

34:50.879 --> 34:52.172
You should just drop this case.

34:53.048 --> 34:55.593
You were only just transferred here

34:55.926 --> 34:59.013
and I'm worried you'll be
shipped out again just as fast.

34:59.597 --> 35:00.598
And besides, right now...

35:04.727 --> 35:06.061
HAN GYEONG-WOOK

35:12.943 --> 35:15.154
A SPECIAL TOURISM ZONE WILL
REVITALIZE YEONGSEON ISLAND

35:20.326 --> 35:21.785
Han Gyeong-wook!

35:21.869 --> 35:23.579
- Han Gyeong-wook!
- Han Gyeong-wook!

35:23.662 --> 35:25.289
-Han Gyeong-wook!
-Han Gyeong-wook!

35:25.372 --> 35:27.166
- Han Gyeong-wook!
- Han Gyeong-wook!

35:27.249 --> 35:28.917
- Han Gyeong-wook!
- Han Gyeong-wook!

35:29.001 --> 35:30.502
-Han Gyeong-wook!
-Han Gyeong-wook!

35:31.003 --> 35:32.463
-Han Gyeong-wook!
-Han Gyeong-wook!

35:32.880 --> 35:34.214
-Han Gyeong-wook!
-Han Gyeong-wook!

35:50.731 --> 35:52.858
I've identified the owner of the
motorcycle you mentioned yesterday.

35:53.108 --> 35:54.109
But the owner...

35:54.360 --> 35:57.404
is a high school student with no
connection to Bulgae or North Korea.

36:05.371 --> 36:07.122
I'm done. I'll get it.

36:10.626 --> 36:12.336
Where are you going?
You were in the middle of peeling onions.

36:16.298 --> 36:17.549
I'm going to go drum up some business.

36:17.633 --> 36:19.259
- We need to increase sales.
- All of a sudden?

36:19.343 --> 36:20.844
Hey, Jeong Ho-myeong!

36:21.220 --> 36:22.221
Hey!

36:29.770 --> 36:30.854
You little...

36:34.525 --> 36:35.859
We're just here to check something

36:35.943 --> 36:37.778
so let's not make this difficult for each
other.

36:38.112 --> 36:39.405
Make sure Chairman Do
doesn't hear about this.

36:39.488 --> 36:41.240
- You know what I mean?
- Yes.

36:42.199 --> 36:44.284
Kang-sik, give this kid
some money for medicine.

36:45.494 --> 36:47.663
Hurry up and find him. This isn't a game.

36:48.205 --> 36:49.998
- Boss!
- All right, Kang-sik found him.

36:50.374 --> 36:51.458
No, that's not it.

36:52.292 --> 36:53.293
Look at the lobby here.

36:54.670 --> 36:55.671
This guy.

36:56.004 --> 36:57.005
Isn't that Ma Gong-bok?

36:57.631 --> 36:58.632
Ma Gong-bok?

37:01.009 --> 37:02.886
Gong-bok showed up after ten years?

37:03.429 --> 37:04.722
On an island like this, of all places?

37:06.181 --> 37:07.433
Hey, Boss! We found him.

37:07.933 --> 37:08.934
It's that guy! That guy right there!

37:17.276 --> 37:18.569
Is this really him?

37:19.528 --> 37:21.405
He's so scrawny.
He looks like he couldn't hurt a fly.

37:22.114 --> 37:23.615
Oh, that's him all right, Boss.

37:27.494 --> 37:28.495
Hey, hey, hey!

37:30.789 --> 37:32.374
The guy who beat up my son

37:32.458 --> 37:34.460
and Gong-bok showed up on the same day?

37:42.426 --> 37:46.054
YEONGSEON POLICE SUBSTATION

37:48.015 --> 37:49.349
- Aren't you going on patrol?
- What?

37:50.350 --> 37:51.393
MY CASH COW

37:52.311 --> 37:54.104
You guys go on ahead.

38:03.781 --> 38:05.657
Yes, hello?

38:05.741 --> 38:07.409
Hey, Officer Kim, how have you been?

38:07.659 --> 38:09.495
I'm doing well, thanks to you.

38:09.828 --> 38:11.330
So, what can I do for you?

38:11.413 --> 38:14.291
A small problem came up
at one of my businesses

38:14.374 --> 38:15.876
and I need you to look into something.

38:16.168 --> 38:17.669
I'm going to send you a few pictures.

38:17.753 --> 38:19.379
I need you to track down these two guys.

38:19.463 --> 38:21.173
If you look through the footage
from the road

38:21.256 --> 38:23.133
near the Heaven Hotel
around 3 o'clock yesterday

38:23.217 --> 38:24.468
it shouldn't be hard
to trace their movements.

38:24.551 --> 38:26.970
Okay. Please send the pictures.

38:35.771 --> 38:37.022
MY CASH COW

38:40.776 --> 38:43.111
YEONGSEON STEEL

39:02.965 --> 39:04.049
Manager Bong.

39:04.424 --> 39:06.134
Why did you skip work
yesterday without notice?

39:06.885 --> 39:07.886
Manager Lee.

39:08.095 --> 39:09.429
I'm so sorry.

39:10.222 --> 39:12.099
It must have been tough for you since I
was gone without a word, right?

39:14.518 --> 39:17.145
I covered for you and told the boss you
took a scheduled day off.

39:18.605 --> 39:20.274
- Manager Lee.
- There must be a reason

39:20.357 --> 39:22.025
why someone who's never done this before
would suddenly skip work.

39:23.694 --> 39:25.779
Thank you.
I'll be sure to repay you for this.

39:26.154 --> 39:27.155
But...

39:27.531 --> 39:29.157
why were you out yesterday?

39:29.658 --> 39:30.659
And your face...

39:32.953 --> 39:34.037
Well...

39:34.580 --> 39:36.206
Manager Lee, in your opinion

39:36.290 --> 39:38.667
what do you think I did
when I was younger?

39:39.334 --> 39:40.335
What you did?

39:46.425 --> 39:48.010
Didn't you work at a car wash?

39:48.093 --> 39:49.803
You're so good at washing cars.

39:49.887 --> 39:51.763
No, not that.

39:54.474 --> 39:55.642
Just take a good look.

39:56.476 --> 39:57.603
Does anything come to mind?

39:58.145 --> 40:01.106
Like a certain
vibe I give off or something.

40:03.525 --> 40:04.526
- One.
- Oh my.

40:07.321 --> 40:08.322
- Two.
- What...

40:11.199 --> 40:12.242
One.

40:15.746 --> 40:16.997
- Manager Bong.
- Two.

40:19.374 --> 40:20.834
- What are you doing?
- I wasn't doing anything.

40:20.918 --> 40:21.960
Are you crazy?

40:22.336 --> 40:23.420
I'm not crazy, but...

40:26.673 --> 40:27.758
Go wash the car.

40:28.342 --> 40:29.843
Since you didn't do it yesterday.
Make it spotless.

40:30.177 --> 40:31.178
Yes, sir.

40:46.526 --> 40:48.946
How dare you? Taking a day off
without my permission?

40:49.446 --> 40:51.782
Manager Bong. When you take a day off

40:51.949 --> 40:54.576
from now on,
you get my permission first. Got it?

41:13.387 --> 41:14.388
Smack!

41:19.893 --> 41:21.520
When the hero is in danger

41:21.603 --> 41:23.397
their past just suddenly
comes flashing back.

41:41.707 --> 41:42.916
Boss!

41:55.512 --> 41:57.597
Boss. I need to take a half day.

41:58.181 --> 41:59.558
You told me to ask first.

41:59.766 --> 42:01.018
So I'm telling you, I'm taking one.

42:04.187 --> 42:05.188
A half day.

42:07.357 --> 42:08.400
Fine, take it.

42:10.068 --> 42:11.069
A half day.

42:21.288 --> 42:22.581
Seriously? Is this it?

42:24.041 --> 42:25.542
We take bank transfers too.

42:27.502 --> 42:28.587
Answer carefully.

42:28.712 --> 42:29.921
Excuse me, fellas.

42:32.632 --> 42:33.884
Can I ask you guys something?

42:33.967 --> 42:35.761
What is it? I'm busy. Can't you see?

42:36.011 --> 42:37.220
You don't look that busy.

42:38.221 --> 42:39.806
Enough with the tough-guy act.

42:39.890 --> 42:41.475
Just answer my question.

42:41.933 --> 42:44.186
Which one of you is Kim Jin-su?

42:48.315 --> 42:49.316
That's me.

42:54.613 --> 42:55.822
Kim Jin-su.

42:58.575 --> 43:00.952
This isn't the guy I saw
on the motorcycle.

43:02.788 --> 43:04.289
So you're Jin-su.

43:05.332 --> 43:06.708
- Jin-su.
- Yeah?

43:07.459 --> 43:08.710
You own a motorcycle, right?

43:08.919 --> 43:10.337
Did you happen to lend
that motorcycle to anyone?

43:10.420 --> 43:11.630
And why should I tell you?

43:11.755 --> 43:12.881
Could you please tell me?

43:12.964 --> 43:14.508
It's really important that I find out.

43:14.633 --> 43:16.593
If it's that important to you

43:16.885 --> 43:18.095
then you should offer something for it.

43:18.428 --> 43:19.429
You expect it for free?

43:21.973 --> 43:22.974
Hold him.

43:27.104 --> 43:29.064
All right, let's see what you've got.

43:29.147 --> 43:30.982
If I like what I see, I'll tell you.

43:31.316 --> 43:34.361
Jeez, what should I do?
I don't have any money

43:34.903 --> 43:36.404
but I can give you something else.

43:45.831 --> 43:47.207
- Jin-su.
- Hey.

43:50.293 --> 43:52.379
Hey, what are you doing? Get him! Hurry!

43:52.712 --> 43:53.713
You!

44:11.606 --> 44:13.441
When an adult asks you a question

44:13.733 --> 44:16.611
you answer. Where are your manners?

44:17.445 --> 44:21.032
- Trying to throw a punch at me?
- Sir! Sir!

44:21.116 --> 44:22.742
It hurts!

44:28.790 --> 44:30.041
- Jin-su.
- Yes.

44:30.750 --> 44:32.919
- I'm going to ask you one more time.
- Yes.

44:33.253 --> 44:34.629
You own a motorcycle, right?

44:34.713 --> 44:35.797
That shiny one.

44:36.006 --> 44:37.883
- You mean my Scooter?
- Yes, that's the one. Your Scooter.

44:39.551 --> 44:41.052
That punk Heo Nam-il took it.

44:41.386 --> 44:42.387
Why?

44:42.846 --> 44:44.014
- Heo Nam-il?
- Yes.

44:47.976 --> 44:50.020
Is this guy trying to
drive me into the ground?

44:56.026 --> 44:57.611
Orthostatic hypotension...

45:19.090 --> 45:20.091
Are you all right?

45:21.968 --> 45:22.969
I'm sorry.

45:25.764 --> 45:27.182
When did you get here?

45:28.642 --> 45:29.851
Just now.

45:31.102 --> 45:32.771
- But are you not feeling well?
- No, it's just...

45:32.938 --> 45:33.939
Well...

45:34.022 --> 45:35.482
I just...

45:35.899 --> 45:37.400
haven't been sleeping well lately.

45:38.360 --> 45:39.361
I'm sorry.

45:48.453 --> 45:49.829
Do you have the lunch box there?

45:49.913 --> 45:51.122
Lunch box? Oh, yes.

45:51.206 --> 45:52.415
Just a moment.

46:02.008 --> 46:03.385
- It's fried chicken with sweet sauce.
- Yes.

46:13.895 --> 46:15.230
Oh, please...

46:16.022 --> 46:18.149
don't feel obligated.

46:18.483 --> 46:21.945
Luckily what you mentioned was available

46:22.028 --> 46:23.280
so I decided to order it.

46:24.239 --> 46:25.407
It's...

46:26.283 --> 46:28.201
It's what we do for our regulars.

46:32.706 --> 46:34.165
You said you weren't sleeping well, right?

46:36.167 --> 46:37.794
Can you hold out your hand for me?

46:43.174 --> 46:44.968
This is how you do it for handcuffs.

46:45.468 --> 46:46.720
My arm's a bit numb.

46:48.054 --> 46:49.055
No, like this.

46:49.306 --> 46:50.307
Like this.

46:55.687 --> 46:59.107
This is what I have
when I'm on my night rounds

46:59.941 --> 47:01.735
and it works pretty well.

47:03.361 --> 47:05.322
Have some. It'll help you wake up.

47:06.072 --> 47:07.073
Okay.

47:10.201 --> 47:11.202
Thank you.

47:11.870 --> 47:12.912
Thank you, too.

47:18.918 --> 47:19.919
Goodbye.

47:21.087 --> 47:22.130
Bye.

47:23.340 --> 47:24.341
Take care.

47:51.868 --> 47:53.078
She said thanks.

48:05.673 --> 48:06.674
What?

48:14.641 --> 48:17.560
You said you couldn't sleep
and felt like you were dying

48:17.644 --> 48:19.521
so I dropped everything and rushed over.

48:19.854 --> 48:22.232
- You look just fine.
- Can't you see these dark circles?

48:22.732 --> 48:24.025
Forget it. You should go home.

48:25.026 --> 48:26.444
You must be exhausted
for all sorts of reasons.

48:26.528 --> 48:28.488
Who's the one who ditched work

48:28.571 --> 48:29.697
and ran off in the first place?

48:30.907 --> 48:32.575
Did I go out and mess around like you did?

48:33.493 --> 48:35.286
Our business that you don't care about

48:35.370 --> 48:36.746
our real business!

48:37.747 --> 48:40.625
I was doing that while you were
goofing off with that woman!

48:40.917 --> 48:42.627
You little punk.

48:49.259 --> 48:50.260
Go ahead.

48:50.635 --> 48:51.636
Hit me.

48:52.679 --> 48:55.056
I'd love to take a good punch for a
change. Go on, hit me.

48:55.890 --> 48:56.891
Hit me.

49:03.273 --> 49:05.442
Let's cool off and talk about this later.

49:08.945 --> 49:10.363
You can't even hit me anymore?

49:12.532 --> 49:13.658
You know...

49:14.451 --> 49:16.786
I don't care about Gang Beom-ryong,
the owner of the Kind Convenience Store.

49:16.870 --> 49:19.122
I miss my old reckless boss

49:20.290 --> 49:22.459
Gang Beom-ryong from the Hwasan Sect.

49:22.959 --> 49:24.043
It's not working. Damn it.

49:44.147 --> 49:47.025
Gong-bok and Beom-ryong.
Those bastards show up after ten years

49:47.108 --> 49:48.526
and screw up my business?

49:49.986 --> 49:51.279
I should've just
finished them off back then.

49:54.532 --> 49:55.533
But, Boss...

49:56.075 --> 49:57.911
The guy who did this to us...

49:58.119 --> 50:01.623
do you really think he's connected to
Beom-ryong and Gong-bok?

50:01.956 --> 50:04.375
How dare you still
call his name so nicely?

50:05.793 --> 50:07.045
Look.

50:07.712 --> 50:09.297
Do you think it's a coincidence
that Gong-bok was there

50:09.380 --> 50:11.090
while you were getting beaten up?

50:12.133 --> 50:14.219
That bastard Gang Beom-ryong got rid of
Chairman Hwang Hwa-san

50:14.302 --> 50:15.845
to take his place, and now he's after me.

50:16.012 --> 50:18.097
He must've hired
some martial arts master or something.

50:19.557 --> 50:22.185
He can't fight me one-on-one like before,
so he pulls this kind of crap.

50:26.689 --> 50:30.693
This scar aches whenever it rains. I think
it's time for revenge.

50:31.569 --> 50:33.655
Boss, we heard from Sergeant Kim.

50:33.905 --> 50:35.823
-They've located both of them.
-Okay.

50:36.324 --> 50:38.034
- Everyone, get ready.
- Yes, Boss.

50:43.748 --> 50:44.916
Let's go!

50:44.999 --> 50:46.292
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

50:50.797 --> 50:51.798
So...

50:53.633 --> 50:56.302
- you got hit and your memory came back?
- No, before I got hit.

50:56.803 --> 50:59.180
I felt the baseball coming at me
from behind, and suddenly

50:59.264 --> 51:01.724
this scene just flashed through my mind.

51:03.351 --> 51:04.602
When I was younger...

51:05.728 --> 51:07.564
I had a six-pack

51:08.565 --> 51:09.857
and I kicked a dagger

51:09.941 --> 51:11.818
flying at me from behind!

51:12.527 --> 51:14.779
- You kicked a dagger? Come on.
- I'm serious!

51:15.363 --> 51:17.115
Try to hit me. Come on.

51:19.867 --> 51:20.868
Okay.

51:21.869 --> 51:23.246
I'll feel it coming and dodge.

51:34.382 --> 51:35.883
- Boss...
- Are they here?

51:35.967 --> 51:38.011
- Yes, they're here.
- Get in there, quickly!

51:38.094 --> 51:39.095
What the...

51:41.723 --> 51:43.224
So you little rats

51:43.308 --> 51:44.726
were hiding here, huh?

51:45.518 --> 51:46.853
What's this? Are you bowing to me?

51:53.192 --> 51:54.485
Hey, what's going on?

51:54.569 --> 51:55.570
What's this?

51:55.653 --> 51:56.904
What's going on?

51:57.238 --> 51:58.615
Hold on, it's not that.

51:58.698 --> 51:59.699
Wait a minute.

52:00.700 --> 52:02.327
What's going on?

52:02.410 --> 52:04.621
Did they know we were
coming or something? Damn it.

52:08.583 --> 52:09.584
Hey, hold on.

52:11.336 --> 52:12.754
Hold on.

52:20.345 --> 52:22.347
Damn, you scared me! Hey, get him!

52:22.680 --> 52:23.806
Hey, get that bastard!

52:24.182 --> 52:25.433
Jeez, you scared me.

52:34.984 --> 52:36.444
Welcome to Jumbo Convenience Store.

52:54.295 --> 52:55.505
Long time no see, Gong-bok.

53:15.692 --> 53:17.568
ORAN CHINESE RESTAURANT

53:35.086 --> 53:36.754
Your food delivery is here.

53:38.923 --> 53:40.133
I'm coming in.

54:14.917 --> 54:16.544
The place is a mess.

54:16.627 --> 54:19.213
Someone might've beaten me to it.

54:23.509 --> 54:25.470
Yeongseon Steel.

54:29.640 --> 54:31.392
YEONGSEON FOOD

54:31.476 --> 54:32.769
Yeongseon...

54:33.478 --> 54:34.479
Food.

54:45.198 --> 54:46.449
You know...

54:46.532 --> 54:48.910
I don't care about Gang Beom-ryong,
the owner of the Kind Convenience Store.

54:49.285 --> 54:51.704
I miss my old reckless boss

54:52.705 --> 54:55.166
Gang Beom-ryong from the Hwasan Sect.

55:00.963 --> 55:02.215
Damn it.

55:13.893 --> 55:15.186
MA GONG-BOK

55:21.484 --> 55:23.903
MA GONG-BOK

55:25.196 --> 55:26.405
Hey, Gong-bok?

55:26.489 --> 55:28.783
Well, Beom-ryong, it's been a while.

55:29.784 --> 55:32.286
- Who is this?
- You don't recognize my voice?

55:32.537 --> 55:33.871
Come on, that hurts.

55:34.163 --> 55:35.164
It's me. In-gu.

55:37.875 --> 55:40.169
- How could you...
- We old Hwasan Sect guys

55:40.503 --> 55:41.712
should get together and catch up.

55:42.505 --> 55:44.340
I'll text you the location.

55:44.715 --> 55:46.384
Don't be late.

55:46.717 --> 55:48.636
I'm dying to see you.

55:48.719 --> 55:51.430
Boss, Beom-ryong, please help me.

55:57.895 --> 56:00.815
DON'T MAKE ME ANY ANGRIER

56:45.484 --> 56:47.278
Now I'm sure of it.

56:47.945 --> 56:49.322
The man who was in this house...

56:56.746 --> 56:57.997
is the missing Bulgae.

56:59.290 --> 57:02.043
Come on. I'm not asking
for anything difficult.

57:02.668 --> 57:04.462
I just asked you to find someone

57:04.545 --> 57:06.464
who worked with Han Gyeong-wook.

57:06.547 --> 57:07.548
Is that really so difficult?

57:07.632 --> 57:09.091
Do you want to get someone fired?

57:09.300 --> 57:11.886
Han Gyeong-wook used to work here.

57:12.011 --> 57:14.263
Do you have any idea how many connections
he still has in this company?

57:14.388 --> 57:16.140
He quit to get into politics.

57:16.223 --> 57:17.725
I'm sure those connections are long gone.

57:17.808 --> 57:19.226
They're still as strong as ever.

57:19.310 --> 57:20.311
Look, I'm hanging up.

57:20.478 --> 57:21.938
Don't drag me into your mess.

57:22.021 --> 57:23.856
No, wait. Just one more question. That's
it.

57:24.148 --> 57:26.776
- Just one more question.
- Get up, you hear me?

57:27.151 --> 57:28.152
This son of a bitch.

57:28.319 --> 57:29.987
Who the hell is this guy?

57:34.367 --> 57:36.535
Jeez, just tell us already.

57:37.912 --> 57:39.121
Hey. Who do you work for?

57:39.997 --> 57:41.791
I'm just his uncle.

57:42.833 --> 57:44.460
So you're not going to talk, huh?

57:45.795 --> 57:47.171
Well, you leave me no choice.

57:47.254 --> 57:49.006
I'm going to ask you some questions.

57:50.049 --> 57:51.509
And if I don't like your answers

57:51.592 --> 57:53.094
or you piss me off...

57:53.177 --> 57:54.679
you'll get the bat.

57:55.346 --> 57:56.931
So think carefully before you answer.

57:59.308 --> 58:00.476
You son of a bitch.

58:01.811 --> 58:03.145
Let's start with you, Gong-bok.

58:04.981 --> 58:07.066
You bastard, why'd you suddenly show up?

58:07.233 --> 58:09.694
I was just minding my own business at the
convenience store.

58:10.152 --> 58:13.072
You're the one who showed up
out of nowhere, you bastard, Yoo In-gu.

58:13.155 --> 58:14.407
Has this bastard lost his mind?

58:16.117 --> 58:18.285
Gong-bok, let's think about this
logically.

58:18.703 --> 58:22.373
Right when I'm trying to start a new
business on Yeongseon Island...

58:23.082 --> 58:25.960
at my business, Heaven Capital, which
that bastard destroyed

58:26.377 --> 58:27.878
you showed up with him.

58:28.587 --> 58:31.048
And you're telling me you're just an
innocent convenience store clerk?

58:31.132 --> 58:32.383
Is this all just a coincidence?

58:33.134 --> 58:34.385
Does that make any sense to you?

58:34.468 --> 58:36.721
I don't know
anything about it, you bastard.

58:39.140 --> 58:40.558
That's not the answer I wanted.

58:41.142 --> 58:42.143
Hey, get him up.

58:44.520 --> 58:45.604
Hurry.

58:50.026 --> 58:51.235
Come on, get him up.

58:51.318 --> 58:52.570
This bastard.

58:53.821 --> 58:54.989
We've got a customer.

59:29.523 --> 59:30.524
TWO NATIONAL INTELLIGENCE SERVICE AGENTS
CAUGHT COLLUDING WITH NORTH KOREA...

59:30.608 --> 59:33.611
THE MURDER OF DIRECTOR KWON SOON-BOK
GANG LEADER HWANG HWA-SAN IMPLICATED

59:34.779 --> 59:36.072
Ten years ago...

59:36.489 --> 59:38.032
the National Intelligence Service agents

59:38.115 --> 59:40.701
and the spy on the passenger ferry?

59:41.577 --> 59:43.329
Yes, that's the one.

59:44.371 --> 59:45.831
Who was in charge of it?

59:47.291 --> 59:48.501
Deputy Chief Han Gyeong-wook.

59:48.584 --> 59:49.919
Han Gyeong-wook?

59:51.629 --> 59:53.255
Oh, Han Gyeong-wook...

59:53.506 --> 59:55.800
Around that same time...

59:56.133 --> 59:59.970
he also arrested the culprit in the
murder of Director Kwon Soon-bok.

01:00:00.054 --> 01:00:02.431
- So, could these two cases be connected?
- Hey.

01:00:02.723 --> 01:00:04.016
That's all I can say.

01:00:04.558 --> 01:00:06.811
This case is classified.
It's orders from the top.

01:00:08.229 --> 01:00:10.356
This isn't like the other cases
you've handled.

01:00:10.731 --> 01:00:12.024
It's on a completely different level.

01:00:12.650 --> 01:00:14.401
Drop it now before you get hurt.

01:00:21.325 --> 01:00:22.743
Yes, Chief Kim.

01:00:24.203 --> 01:00:26.956
- What?
- He just suddenly crossed into my lane...

01:00:27.456 --> 01:00:30.084
- hit me, and just drove off.
- What about the other vehicle?

01:00:30.167 --> 01:00:32.169
I ran the plates...

01:00:32.628 --> 01:00:33.754
but it's a ghost car.

01:00:34.588 --> 01:00:35.840
A ghost car?

01:00:39.093 --> 01:00:41.554
Uncle. This is a dangerous situation.

01:00:41.637 --> 01:00:42.972
Do it already!

01:00:43.055 --> 01:00:44.431
Agent 007.

01:00:44.515 --> 01:00:46.267
I don't know! Just be quiet a minute.

01:00:50.187 --> 01:00:51.230
Just a second.

01:00:51.981 --> 01:00:53.357
Don't you have to get hit for it to work?

01:00:53.941 --> 01:00:54.942
Are you crazy?

01:00:55.025 --> 01:00:56.152
You're telling me to take a punch?

01:00:57.111 --> 01:00:58.696
- I'm still hurting from before.
- Hey!

01:00:59.280 --> 01:01:00.489
You two are next

01:01:00.573 --> 01:01:01.907
so keep your mouths shut.

01:01:10.166 --> 01:01:12.668
Man, this guy's tough.
He just won't break.

01:01:13.460 --> 01:01:16.130
You're dead when Beom-ryong gets here,
you son of a bitch.

01:01:16.213 --> 01:01:18.090
Yeah? But I looked into it

01:01:18.757 --> 01:01:21.510
and this Gang Beom-ryong has been a
convenience store owner for ten years.

01:01:22.094 --> 01:01:23.679
A guy who's done nothing but scan barcodes
for a decade...

01:01:24.555 --> 01:01:25.931
you think he's still got his old moves?

01:01:53.167 --> 01:01:54.960
All right, let's move
on to the next in line.

01:01:55.586 --> 01:01:56.837
Hey, Mr. Martial Arts Master.

01:01:58.839 --> 01:02:01.175
Did those guys hire you
to beat my son to a pulp?

01:02:01.258 --> 01:02:02.718
Wait, sir.

01:02:02.801 --> 01:02:04.595
Hired? No, I'm just...

01:02:04.929 --> 01:02:06.722
an ordinary office worker.

01:02:06.805 --> 01:02:08.307
Just a regular salaryman.

01:02:08.766 --> 01:02:10.768
He's not a Martial Arts Master,
he's a comedian.

01:02:11.352 --> 01:02:12.436
You're sure he's the one who beat you?

01:02:12.519 --> 01:02:13.646
Yes, boss, I'm telling you.

01:02:13.979 --> 01:02:15.981
He took one hit and passed out, but then

01:02:16.357 --> 01:02:18.359
he slowly got up like a zombie

01:02:18.567 --> 01:02:21.028
rolled his eyes back,
and went totally berserk. I swear.

01:02:23.030 --> 01:02:24.156
Um, excuse me.

01:02:25.908 --> 01:02:27.034
Go on and hit him.

01:02:28.827 --> 01:02:30.829
- Go on, just hit him once!
- Are you insane?

01:02:30.913 --> 01:02:32.373
What is he, the Hulk?
He transforms when you hit him?

01:02:32.456 --> 01:02:34.166
No! Sir, it's not like that.

01:02:34.333 --> 01:02:35.584
Are you out of your mind?

01:02:35.876 --> 01:02:37.920
- It's okay, trust me.
- Look at these two, having fun.

01:02:38.504 --> 01:02:39.505
Hey, go ahead and hit him.

01:02:42.174 --> 01:02:43.425
Are you sure this is okay?

01:02:43.509 --> 01:02:45.344
- Should I do it?
- No. I'll do it.

01:02:51.392 --> 01:02:52.518
What the hell?

01:02:52.935 --> 01:02:54.353
Don't get smart with me! Dammit!

01:02:54.436 --> 01:02:57.147
Hey, you idiot! Is that the best you can
do? Hit him harder!

01:02:57.231 --> 01:02:58.232
That was plenty hard...

01:03:01.277 --> 01:03:02.278
Uncle!

01:03:09.785 --> 01:03:11.036
- Uncle!
- Look.

01:03:11.453 --> 01:03:12.454
There it is!

01:03:14.373 --> 01:03:17.543
It hurts so much.

01:03:19.545 --> 01:03:20.546
Uncle...

01:03:23.257 --> 01:03:24.258
Uncle!

01:03:26.969 --> 01:03:28.345
It hurts so much.

01:03:28.429 --> 01:03:31.265
I keep telling you, I'm
just a regular office worker.

01:03:32.308 --> 01:03:33.809
Hey! Stomp him!

01:03:34.226 --> 01:03:35.477
Hey, wait!

01:04:02.755 --> 01:04:03.922
Hey, Ma Gong-bok

01:04:04.006 --> 01:04:06.675
did your precious
convenience store boss run off?

01:04:06.759 --> 01:04:08.510
Why isn't he showing up, huh?

01:04:09.386 --> 01:04:11.638
He's supposed to be getting
revenge for this scar.

01:04:20.105 --> 01:04:21.231
I guess there's no choice.

01:04:22.399 --> 01:04:23.484
You'll have to be the next best thing.

01:04:24.193 --> 01:04:25.861
So I guess I'll have to
take it out on you.

01:04:43.837 --> 01:04:44.838
What the hell?

01:05:30.092 --> 01:05:31.301
Boss!

01:05:34.555 --> 01:05:36.598
- Gang Beom-ryong, that bastard.
- You bastard.

01:05:38.142 --> 01:05:39.685
I haven't slept in two days

01:05:39.768 --> 01:05:41.103
and I'm freaking exhausted.

01:05:42.396 --> 01:05:43.439
Ma Gong-bok.

01:05:45.524 --> 01:05:47.609
Let's wrap this up quick and get out of
here.

01:05:57.995 --> 01:06:00.456
FIFTIES PROFESSIONALS

01:06:12.050 --> 01:06:13.886
Seriously, what do you think you're doing?

01:06:14.219 --> 01:06:15.554
You think I enjoyed living like this?

01:06:15.679 --> 01:06:18.223
This is all your fault, Jeong Ho-myeong.

01:06:18.432 --> 01:06:20.517
Hard-working citizens like yourself...

01:06:20.601 --> 01:06:22.478
that's who cops like me
are supposed to protect.

01:06:24.396 --> 01:06:26.648
No matter how pure it is

01:06:26.732 --> 01:06:28.859
it only takes a few storms
to turn the water muddy...

01:06:29.234 --> 01:06:31.612
- It happens in an instant.
- I don't understand. Why?

01:06:31.820 --> 01:06:33.655
Something's definitely off.
This whole thing smells fishy.

01:06:34.239 --> 01:06:36.283
Be careful.
This is your first mission in ten years.

01:06:36.366 --> 01:06:38.076
Oh, come on!

01:06:38.160 --> 01:06:39.411
Have you forgotten who I am?

01:06:39.745 --> 01:06:41.205
Don't let his looks fool you.

01:06:41.288 --> 01:06:43.290
He's the top black ops agent
for the National Intelligence Service.
